{
  "reason": "The current 0.7399 plateau comes from a homogeneous entity-embedding MLP ensemble that must implicitly rediscover strong coupon×customer interaction structure from only ~8k rows; historical TE experiments show the representation gap is real, while failures were caused by fold ownership and bundle-persistence wiring rather than the encode idea itself. The initial plan correctly targets smoothed conditional-acceptance features plus removal of accuracy-hurting label smoothing, so the refinement stays inside the existing MLP backbone and instead hardens fold-safe TE construction, persistence, and read-only predict-time application. Data-processing is the right place for the encoder, and training-evaluation is the right place to wire fold-local TE and sharpen argmax decisions.",
  "module": [
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering",
    "training_evaluation"
  ],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Extend CouponFeatureEngineer with a leakage-safe smoothed target encoder over the existing COMBO_COLS plus raw schema categoricals: add te_maps_, te_prior_, te_m_, and te_col_names_ state, and implement fit_target_encoding(df, y, n_inner=5, m=20, seed=42) plus transform_target_encoding(df). WHY: These conditional P(accept | coupon, occupation, time, expiration, maritalStatus, has_children, income, ...) rates are currently destroyed by ID/ordinal coding; feeding them as dense numerics lets the residual MLP spend capacity on continuous margins instead of relearning categorical splits, and historical TE failures were caused by leakage/persistence, not by the representation idea. HOW: fit_target_encoding builds per-key count/sum tables from the supplied training rows only, uses inner StratifiedKFold OOF assignments for those rows so a row's own label never contributes to its TE value, stores full-train maps_ for later transform, and falls back to prior_ for unseen/NaN keys with smoothing formula (sum_y + prior*m)/(count + m); transform_target_encoding appends the fixed te_col_names_ columns and transform() includes them after the existing numeric block only when te_maps_ is present, never removing existing categorical columns. Keep all existing attributes (label_maps, combo_counts, categorical_cols, feature_names), method names fit/transform/fit_transform, and downstream column-order contracts intact.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Wire the new TE encoder into the existing 5-fold StratifiedKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=42) loop, the full-data N_REFIT refits, bundle persistence, and the read-only predict path, and remove label smoothing from the final accuracy-oriented fits. WHY: TE features are only valid if each fold's training rows see encodings derived without their own labels and validation/predict rows use persisted maps; the historical failed TE attempt was a wiring/persistence problem, and historical successes persisted all encoder state in the bundle and never refit at predict time. HOW: after fe = CouponFeatureEngineer().fit(df_tr) in each fold, call fe.fit_target_encoding(df_tr, y_idx[tr], n_inner=5, m=20, seed=seed+fi) before _prepare_fold(fe, df_tr/df_va); for full refit call fe_full.fit_target_encoding(features, y_idx, n_inner=5, m=20, seed=seed+777); then set cfg.label_smoothing=0.0 in run_training_evaluation for CV and production fits while leaving ModelConfig defaults and all other hyperparameters unchanged. Persist fe (already carried in bundle) including te_maps_/te_prior_/te_m_/te_col_names_, and in run_predict call fe.transform only (never fit_target_encoding), rebuild _prepare_fold/_shift_cat/_apply_norm from the same feature_names order, and apply the unchanged argmax/threshold label-mapping and row_id=0..N-1 output contract."
  }
}
